WEBVTT

00:08:29.299 --> 00:08:31.083
with your crystallized intelligence,

00:08:31.107 --> 00:08:34.037
how you can be the best instructor,
the best synthesizer,

00:08:34.061 --> 00:08:36.005
you can possibly be.

00:08:36.029 --> 00:08:39.373
AG: OK, so this is where
I want to start disagreeing with you.

00:08:39.875 --> 00:08:41.795
So my read of the evidence

00:08:41.819 --> 00:08:45.497
is that people don't inherently
become less creative.

00:08:45.521 --> 00:08:48.271
One of the things that happens
as people's careers advance

00:08:48.295 --> 00:08:49.716
is they tend to produce less,

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:51.823
just, you know,
in terms of overall volume.

00:08:51.847 --> 00:08:53.048
I think it's not ability.

00:08:53.072 --> 00:08:55.021
I think it's motivation that's dropping.

00:08:55.045 --> 00:08:57.783
I think, you know,
a lot of people become complacent

00:08:57.807 --> 00:09:00.232
and they feel like
they've achieved enough success,